                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Dr. Paramita Suklabaidya is Professor in Tourism Management and the former Director of the School of Tourism and Hospitality Services Management (SOTHSM), IGNOU. She is a NET- JRF awardee in Tourism and an alumnus of Delhi University and Lucknow University. She has more than 20 years of teaching experience that started with IGNOU, followed by lecturer in Pondicherry,  Assistant Professor in Banaras Hindu University (BHU), with IITTM, Gwalior and back to IGNOU, New Delhi. </p><p>She has been associated as a Member of various committees like one constituted by - State Education Boards;  CBSE for revising the existing course curriculum on Travel and Tourism; AICTE on National Vocational Education Qualification Framework (NVEQF) for various levels in the field of Tourism Sector as well as for the development of Diploma and Bachelors degree curriculum  in Tourism. She is also a member of Board of Studies (Tourism and Hospitality) for various state and central universities and a resources person for various institutes like National Institute of Technical Teachers Training & Research (Chandigarh), Sushma Swaraj Institute of Foreign Service, National Centre for Good Governance, among others.</p><p>She has given key note address and presented papers in National and International Seminars and Conferences; and has more than 60 publications to her name that includes research papers in referred Journals, chapters in edited books, CBSE books and IGNOU SLM. Till date11 PhD Scholars have submitted their PhD Thesis under her supervision. At present she is the programme co - coordinator of the first Bachelors Degree programme in Facilities Management in the country. She is also involved in the development of courses for Facility Services Management as well as UG Tourism Programme. </p><p>Her Areas of interest include Food Tourism, Tourism Marketing, Rural Tourism, Pink Tourism, Heritage Tourism, Event Management, Visitor Management, Crisis Management in Tourism and Cruises.</p></td>
